-- title:
--   Stability of the q-expansion function field under q↦ q^q in characteristic q
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic a prime $q$, let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $e$ be a Laurent series over $\kappa$. Write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC κ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of $\kappa((X))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC κ Γ`, that is by those Laurent series of the form `intSeriesC κ pf / intSeriesC κ pg`, where for some weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ there are modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and power series $pf, pg$ with integral coefficients satisfying `IsIntegralQExp f pf` and `IsIntegralQExp g pg` (the predicate relating a form to an integral $q$-expansion), with `intSeriesC κ pg ≠ 0`; here `intSeriesC κ p` is the Laurent series obtained from $p$ by reducing its coefficients along $\mathbb{Z} \to \kappa$. The assertion is that if $e$ lies in $F$, then so does [`ModularCurve.qExpand κ q e`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the image of $e$ under the ring homomorphism that rescales the exponent lattice by $q$, i.e. the substitution $\sum_n a_n X^n \mapsto \sum_n a_n X^{qn}$.
--
--   This is the statement that in characteristic $q$ the function field generated by reductions of ratios of integral $q$-expansions is stable under the $q$-power substitution $e(X) \mapsto e(X^q)$, a form of the Frobenius/$q$-expansion compatibility used when comparing modular function fields with their reductions. It is used in the identification of comapped level automorphisms on full-level modular curves, in the lemmas [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.comap_levelAutBar_eq_of_redQ_smul_lineInfty_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.comap_levelAutBar_eq_of_redQ_smul_lineInfty_eq) and its variants for levels two and three.
